"},{"path":"harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-reliability-aggregation.md","content":"# E01 — Deterministic reliability aggregation

## Goal

Extend the existing Agent Dev benefit report with deterministic case-level reliability evidence. Reuse the Agent Dev scenario registry and the in-repository benefit report; do not create a metrics platform.

## Design gate

- The fixture pre-registers `k`, `minCases`, and `flakeThreshold`.
- The design gate is `k = 3` and at least 20 complete cases.
- A case is complete only when all k trials have terminal outcomes. Missing, timeout, crashed, and skipped trials make it incomplete.
- Incomplete cases are reported and excluded from metric denominators.
- `pass^k` means all k trials succeeded. `pass@k` means at least one trial succeeded. They are never aliases.
- A flake is a case whose first trial failed and whose fixed reruns all succeeded. The first failure remains visible.
- Positive anchors must pass every trial. Negative anchors must reject every trial. Any violation fails the gate.
- Safety cases permit neither skips nor flakes.
- Fewer than `minCases` complete cases yields `gate = insufficient-sample`; a small sample is never reported as PASS.

## Acceptance

1. Load the deterministic fixture into the existing benefit report.
2. Report raw denominators, `pass^k`, `pass@k`, flake, every incomplete case, gate, and reasons.
3. Label the oracle as deterministic and state that it does not demonstrate real-provider, human, or generalization results.
4. Do not alter product defaults, product locks, approval semantics, README, dependencies, or automation schedules.
"},{"path":"harness/specs/rules/reliability-aggregation-boundary.md","content":"# Reliability aggregation boundary

The Agent Dev benefit report may aggregate deterministic, pre-registered fixture trials. It must not describe fixture behavior as real model/provider capability, human validation, or generalization.

## Metric boundary

`pass^k` and `pass@k` are distinct metrics. `pass^k` counts a complete case only when every trial succeeds; `pass@k` counts it when at least one trial succeeds. A missing, timed-out, crashed, or skipped case is incomplete: preserve its identity and status, but exclude it from both metric denominators.

The report must expose the raw total, complete, incomplete, and excluded counts. Ratios without a valid denominator are `null`, never zero or a fabricated PASS.

## Failure boundary

The first failed trial cannot be erased by successful reruns. A fixed rerun is a flake, not evidence that the original gate never failed. Safety cases require zero flakes and zero skips. Positive anchors require every trial to pass; negative anchors require every trial to reject. Anchor violations fail the gate.

If complete sample size is below the registered minimum, the gate is `insufficient-sample` unless a hard anchor or safety violation has already failed it.

This report is internal evaluation evidence only. It does not change product configuration, defaults, locks, approval behavior, user-visible APIs, dependencies, or schedules.
"},{"path":"docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/e01-reliability-aggregation.md","content":"# E01 reliability aggregation closure

## Scope

This package adds deterministic reliability aggregation to the existing Agent Dev benefit report. The implementation reuses the Agent Dev scenario registry and adds an offline fixture under `shared/agent-dev/`; no metrics platform or user-visible interface was introduced.

## Deterministic contract

The fixture registers `k = 3`, `minCases = 20`, and a flake threshold before evaluation. It records positive and negative anchors, a safety case, one first-failure/fixed-rerun flake, and explicit missing, timeout, crash, and skip cases.

The report distinguishes:

- `pass^k`: all k trials succeeded;
- `pass@k`: at least one trial succeeded;
- flake: the first trial failed and all fixed reruns succeeded.

Incomplete cases remain visible with their original status and are excluded from metric denominators. Positive anchors must pass every trial, negative anchors must reject every trial, and safety cases must have no skip or flake. The sample-size gate requires at least 20 complete cases.

## Acceptance record

The deterministic fixture is an offline oracle only. It does not establish real-provider behavior, human evaluation, or model generalization.

The change is limited to the internal benefit report, its aggregation helper and type declaration, fixture, and harness/closure documentation. README files are intentionally unchanged because there is no user-visible API, configuration, default, lock, permission, dependency, or approval-semantic change. No automation schedule was added.

The clean-candidate fast gate requires: targeted unit tests; runtime/core type checks; scoped lint; harness validation and dry-run; a credential scan with zero findings; and successful read-back of `SHA256SUMS`. These checks are release-candidate acceptance steps and are not performed by the runtime aggregation implementation.
"},{"path":"scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs","content":"#!/usr/bin/env node
import { existsSync } from 'node:fs';
import { mkdir, readFile, readdir, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';
import { join, resolve } from 'node:path';
import { performance } from 'node:perf_hooks';
import { aggregateReliability } from './lib/reliability-aggregation.mjs';

const ROOT = process.cwd();
const OUT_DIR = resolve(ROOT, 'artifacts/agent-dev-benefit-eval');

async function read(path) {
  return await readFile(resolve(ROOT, path), 'utf8');
}

async function walk(dir, predicate = () => true) {
  const results = [];
  async function visit(abs) {
    for (const entry of await readdir(abs, { withFileTypes: true })) {
      if (entry.name === 'node_modules' || entry.name === '.git' || entry.name === 'dist') continue;
      const full = join(abs, entry.name);
      if (entry.isDirectory()) await visit(full);
      else if (predicate(full)) results.push(full);
    }
  }
  await visit(resolve(ROOT, dir));
  return results;
}

function countMatches(text, pattern) {
  return [...text.matchAll(pattern)].length;
}

function extractScenarioIds(registryText) {
  const match = registryText.match(/export const AGENT_DEV_SCENARIOS = \[([\s\S]*?)\] as const/);
  return match ? [...match[1].matchAll(/\{\s*id:\s*'([^']+)'/g)].map((entry) => entry[1]) : [];
}

function packageInstalled(name) {
  const normalized = name.startsWith('@') ? name.replace('/', '\\') : name;
  return existsSync(resolve(ROOT, 'node_modules', ...normalized.split(/[\\/]/)));
}

async function scanSelectorCoverage() {
  const files = await walk('src', (file) => /\.(tsx|ts)$/.test(file));
  let testIdCount = 0;
  let interactiveTagCount = 0;
  let interactiveWithoutInlineTestId = 0;
  for (const file of files) {
    const text = await readFile(file, 'utf8');
    testIdCount += countMatches(text, /data-testid=/g);
    const tags = [...text.matchAll(/<(?<tag>button|input|select|textarea|a)\b(?<attrs>[^>]*)>/g)];
    interactiveTagCount += tags.length;
    interactiveWithoutInlineTestId += tags.filter((match) => !String(match.groups?.attrs ?? '').includes('data-testid')).length;
  }
  return {
    fileCount: files.length,
    testIdCount,
    interactiveTagCount,
    interactiveWithoutInlineTestId,
    inlineSelectorCoverage: interactiveTagCount === 0
      ? 1
      : Number(((interactiveTagCount - interactiveWithoutInlineTestId) / interactiveTagCount).toFixed(3)),
  };
}

function formatRate(metric) {
  return metric.rate === null ? 'n/a' : `${(metric.rate * 100).toFixed(1)}% (${metric.numerator}/${metric.denominator})`;
}

function renderMarkdown(report) {
  const tools = report.externalTools.map((tool) => (
    `| ${tool.package} | ${tool.installed ? 'yes' : 'no'} | ${tool.role} |`
  )).join('\n');
  const reliability = report.reliability;
  const incomplete = reliability.incomplete.map((item) => (
    `| ${item.id} | ${item.scenarioId ?? 'n/a'} | ${item.status} | ${item.trialCount}/${item.expectedTrials} |`
  )).join('\n') || '| none | n/a | n/a | n/a |';
  const anchors = [
    ...reliability.anchors.positive.map((item) => `| positive | ${item.id} | ${item.pass ? 'pass' : 'fail'} |`),
    ...reliability.anchors.negative.map((item) => `| negative | ${item.id} | ${item.pass ? 'pass' : 'fail'} |`),
  ].join('\n') || '| none | n/a | n/a |';
  return `# Agent Dev Benefit Evaluation

Generated: ${report.generatedAt}

## Summary

| Metric | Value |
| --- | ---: |
| Dev scenarios | ${report.agentDev.scenarioCount} |
| hostApi.agentDev methods | ${report.agentDev.hostApiMethodCount} |
| E2E agent-dev helpers | ${report.agentDev.e2eHelperCount} |
| Runtime schema assertions | ${report.agentDev.schemaAssertionCount} |
| Basic a11y rule families | ${report.quality.a11yRuleCount} |
| Renderer files scanned | ${report.selectorCoverage.fileCount} |
| data-testid occurrences | ${report.selectorCoverage.testIdCount} |
| Interactive tags scanned | ${report.selectorCoverage.interactiveTagCount} |
| Inline selector coverage | ${Math.round(report.selectorCoverage.inlineSelectorCoverage * 100)}% |

## External Tool Readiness

| Package | Installed | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
${tools}

## Deterministic Reliability Aggregation

Oracle: **${reliability.oracle}**. This offline fixture is not evidence from a real provider, real people, or generalization.

Registered design: k=${reliability.design.k}, minimum complete cases=${reliability.design.minCases}, flake threshold=${reliability.design.flakeThreshold}.

| Metric | Result |
| --- | ---: |
| Raw cases | ${reliability.rawDenominator.totalCases} |
| Complete cases | ${reliability.rawDenominator.completeCases} |
| Incomplete cases (excluded from denominators) | ${reliability.rawDenominator.incompleteCases} |
| pass^k | ${formatRate(reliability.metrics.passK)} |
| pass@k | ${formatRate(reliability.metrics.passAtK)} |
| flake | ${formatRate(reliability.metrics.flake)} |
| Gate | **${reliability.gate}** |
| Reasons | ${reliability.reasons.length ? reliability.reasons.join(', ') : 'none'} |

### Preserved Incomplete Cases

| Case | Scenario | Status | Trials |
| --- | --- | --- | ---: |
${incomplete}

### Anchor Aggregation

| Anchor | Case | Result |
| --- | --- | --- |
${anchors}

## Interpretation

- The current in-repo implementation already gives agents ${report.agentDev.scenarioCount} deterministic page entry points and ${report.agentDev.e2eHelperCount} E2E helpers without depending on new packages.
- Schema assertions now reject malformed agent-dev payloads at the Main host-api boundary.
- Basic a11y and visual artifact generation are available through Playwright today; axe/Argos can replace the fallback scanners once supply-chain policy allows installing them.
- The selector coverage metric is a heuristic. It is useful as a trend line, not as a precise accessibility or E2E quality proof.
- The reliability values above describe only the checked-in deterministic fixture and must not be presented as provider, human, or generalization evidence.
`;
}

const start = performance.now();
const [
  scenarioRegistry,
  hostApi,
  e2eFixture,
  schemaText,
  a11yText,
  reliabilityFixture,
] = await Promise.all([
  read('shared/agent-dev/scenarios.ts'),
  read('src/lib/host-api.ts'),
  read('tests/e2e/fixtures/electron.ts'),
  read('shared/host-api/agent-dev-schemas.ts'),
  read('tests/e2e/fixtures/a11y.ts'),
  read('shared/agent-dev/reliability-fixture.json'),
]);

const scenarioIds = extractScenarioIds(scenarioRegistry);
const hostApiAgentDevBlock = hostApi.match(/agentDev:\s*\{([\s\S]*?)\n  \},\n  providers:/)?.[1] ?? '';
const reliability = aggregateReliability(JSON.parse(reliabilityFixture));
const report = {
  generatedAt: new Date().toISOString(),
  durationMs: 0,
  agentDev: {
    scenarioCount: scenarioIds.length,
    scenarios: scenarioIds,
    hostApiMethodCount: countMatches(hostApiAgentDevBlock, /^\s{4}[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*:/gm),
    e2eHelperCount: countMatches(e2eFixture, /export async function (openAgentDevScenario|getAgentDevSnapshot|configureAgentDevHostReplay|getAgentDevHostCalls)/g),
    schemaAssertionCount: countMatches(schemaText, /export function assertAgentDev/g),
  },
  quality: {
    a11yRuleCount: countMatches(a11yText, /add\('([^']+)'/g),
    visualArtifactSpec: existsSync(resolve(ROOT, 'tests/e2e/agent-dev-quality.spec.ts')),
    workbenchScript: existsSync(resolve(ROOT, 'scripts/agent-dev-workbench.mjs')),
  },
  selectorCoverage: await scanSelectorCoverage(),
  reliability,
  externalTools: [
    { package: '@axe-core/playwright', installed: packageInstalled('@axe-core/playwright'), role: 'strict a11y scanning' },
    { package: '@ladle/react', installed: packageInstalled('@ladle/react'), role: 'component scenario workbench' },
    { package: '@argos-ci/playwright', installed: packageInstalled('@argos-ci/playwright'), role: 'hosted visual regression' },
    { package: '@vitest/browser', installed: packageInstalled('@vitest/browser'), role: 'browser component testing' },
    { package: '@testing-library/user-event', installed: packageInstalled('@testing-library/user-event'), role: 'realistic user interactions' },
    { package: 'knip', installed: packageInstalled('knip'), role: 'unused files/deps/exports' },
    { package: 'ajv', installed: packageInstalled('ajv'), role: 'JSON schema validation engine' },
  ],
};
report.durationMs = Number((performance.now() - start).toFixed(1));

await mkdir(OUT_DIR, { recursive: true });
await writeFile(resolve(OUT_DIR, 'report.json'), JSON.stringify(report, null, 2), 'utf8');
await writeFile(resolve(OUT_DIR, 'report.md'), renderMarkdown(report), 'utf8');
console.log(JSON.stringify(report, null, 2));
"}]}
